  "computedNotMeasured": "These are computed ceilings, not wall-meter readings. Continuous draw is the CPU peak plus the GPU total graphics power plus a fixed platform allowance; the recommended supply is the smallest standard size that keeps that draw at or under the target load fraction. Real systems draw less than this most of the time, which is the point: a supply is sized for the ceiling, not the average.",
