    "note": "cpu_peak_watts, not cpu_tdp_watts. TDP is a thermal design figure, not a power limit: AMD allows 1.35x TDP as Package Power Tracking and Intel publishes Maximum Turbo Power as a separate number. Sizing on TDP understates a modern build and is the commonest error in PSU calculators — sizes_missed_by_tdp counts the standard supply sizes it costs, per build, in the pairing table."
